  "question": {
    "text": "In an adiabatic process, the pressure is increased by $\\frac{2}{3} \\% .$ If $\\gamma=\\frac{3}{2},$ then the volume decreases by nearly"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{9} \\%$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3} \\%$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1 \\%$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{9}{4} \\%$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{PV}^{3 / 2}=\\mathrm{K}$\r\n\r\n$\\log \\mathrm{P}+\\frac{3}{2} \\log \\mathrm{V}=\\log \\mathrm{K}$\r\n\r\n$\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{P}}{\\mathrm{P}}+\\frac{3}{2} \\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{V}}=0$\r\n\r\n$\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{V}}=-\\frac{2}{3} \\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{P}}{\\mathrm{P}}$ or $\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{V}}=\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)=-\\frac{4}{9}$"
  }
